<title>PORTUGAL: BA says Portugal flights barely affected by strike.</title>
<headline>BA says Portugal flights barely affected by strike.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-07-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Airways flights to Portugal will be barely affected by a 72-hour cabin crew strike that began on Wednesday, said a statement released by the airline.</p>
<p>&quot;The 0825 flight to Heathrow is the only one of the four daily flights between London and Lisbon that might be altered,&quot; the statement said, adding that BA was prepared to channel passengers to alternative flights on other airlines.</p>
<p>&quot;BA's flights to Oporto (twice daily), Faro (twice daily), and Funchal (three times per week) will be unaffected by the strike,&quot; said the statement.</p>
<p>((--Reuters Lisbon newsroom 3511-353-8254))</p>
